<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8481" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clāmōsus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		clamor (mostly post-Aug.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of clamor</i> or <i>noise</i>, i. e., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>clamoring</i> or <i>bawling continually</i> or <i>loudly</i>, <i>clamorous</i>, <i>noisy</i>, <i>bawling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbidus et clamosus altercator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 6, 4, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pater,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					14, 191</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magister,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					5, 84, 2</span></i>
			.— * <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clāmōsē</span></b> , <i>clamorously</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clamose ne dicamus omnia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 45</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>filled with noise</i>
			or <i>clamor</i>, <i>noisy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 4, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">theatri turba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 5, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">valles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Th. 4, 448</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					9, 144</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 53</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Subura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 18, 2</span></i>
			.—<b>Poet.</b> with <i>gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">undae clamosus Helorus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					14, 269</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Accompanied with noise</i> or <i>clamor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">actio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					5, 3, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phasma Catulli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					8, 186</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adceleratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 3, 13, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortes boum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 4</span></i>
			, pr. 1.</div>
